From 9a9fb3ce8fbfe2b01725e92a9ec04e5facb64af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:07:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: model Mind Blast as 8d8 damage plus confusion

borg_danger() valued a Mind Blast as spell_power / 2 + 1 damage (about
15 for a mind flayer) and ignored its confusion. The spell deals 8d8
(average 36, at most 64) and then confuses for 3+1d4 turns
(monster_spell.txt MIND_BLAST).

Use the maximum damage, as the other spell cases do, and add the same
concern for the confusion that the plain confusion spell gets when the
borg does not resist it.
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..f8090ae34 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -1124,8 +1124,12 @@ static int borg_danger_spell(
             break;
 
         case RSF_MIND_BLAST:
-            if (borg.trait[BI_SAV] < 100)
-                z = (r_ptr->spell_power / 2 + 1);
+            if (borg.trait[BI_SAV] >= 100)
+                break;
+            /* 8d8 damage (monster_spell.txt), then 3+1d4 turns of confusion */
+            z = 8 * 8;
+            if (!borg.trait[BI_RCONF])
+                p += 10;
             break;
 
         case RSF_BRAIN_SMASH:
-- 
2.53.0

